1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,700
How do I organize my life?

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,500
“You are the best nation brought forth for mankind: you enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and believe in Allah.” (Āl ʿImrān 3:110)

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,950
Enjoin what is right. Forbid what is wrong. Believe in Allah.

4
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:14,200
That is what makes us the best.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:21,200
Look at what you already do: five prayers every day, Fajr before the sun, 30 days of fasting, one Qiblah, Zakat, Jumuʿah.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,450
You were made for discipline.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,400
“Indeed, Allah will not change the condition of a people until they change what is within themselves.” (ar-Raʿd 13:11)

8
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,500
The Ummah rises one person at a time.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Ibn al-Qayyim (d. 751 AH) opened his book al-Dāʾ wa al-Dawāʾ with this hadith:

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,200
“Allah has not sent down any disease except that He also sent down its cure.” (Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī 5678)

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,400
The heart has its illnesses too, and every one has a cure.

12
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:40,400
In al-Fawāʾid, he traces how a habit is born:

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,400
a passing thought…

14
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,400
a thought you dwell on…

15
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,400
a desire…

16
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:44,400
resolve…

17
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,400
an action…

18
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,600
a habit.

19
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,800
“If you do not counter it with its opposite, it becomes a habit, and then it is hard for you to leave it.” (al-Fawāʾid, p. 45)

20
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:59,400
Build your day around the five prayers.

21
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:01,400
The prayers are the anchors. Fill the space between them with purpose.

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,300
“The most beloved deeds to Allah are the most consistent ones, even if they are small.” (al-Bukhārī & Muslim)

23
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,300
“Wasting time is worse than death, because it cuts you off from Allah and the Hereafter, while death cuts you off from this world and its people.” (Ibn al-Qayyim, al-Fawāʾid, p. 44)

24
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,600
Your time is your life. Spend it on purpose.

25
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:16,800
Start today.

26
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:17,900
One small deed at a time.

27
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:19,000
In shāʾ Allāh.

